   "fix": null,
   "harm": "introducing AddrPolicy alongside existing network and quality filtering parameters creates redundancy and complexity unless all filtering is unified under the policy",
   "hash": "fc1da9ae8d56b08b",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:55:12+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "r:3612547519",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "r:3612547519",
   "kind": "approach",
   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "if we want to add such a generalized concept for filtering, we should implement the current filtering with it as well. E.g. network and filtered params go away and we only have AddrPolicy as param to GetAddr.",
   "request": "",
   "status": "answered",
   "status_by": null,
   "status_note": "reply on record; standing not assessed yet",
   "type": "objection",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/33663#pullrequestreview-3612547519"
  },
  {
   "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
   "at": "2025-12-28",
   "author": "Bicaru20",
   "author_replies": [
    "c:3697274537"
   ],
   "clears_with": "change",
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "introducing a predicate adds unnecessary complexity compared to oversampling or fully unifying all AddrMan filtering",
   "hash": "2002dd875d225bf3",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:55:12+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "c:3695127117",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c:3695127117",
   "kind": "approach",
   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "introducing a predicate feels like adding unnecessary complexity. I believe his solution is cleaner.",
   "request": "",
   "status": "answered",
   "status_by": null,
   "status_note": "reply on record; standing not assessed yet",
   "type": "objection",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/33663#issuecomment-3695127117"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2025-12-28",
   "author": "fjahr",
   "author_replies": [
    "c:3697274537"
   ],
   "clears_with": "change",
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "AddrPolicy introduces overengineering when simpler oversampling or requesting more addresses and trimming would fix underfill",
   "hash": "ed0a4fa4a3d82373",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:55:12+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "r:3614441070",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "r:3614441070",
   "kind": "approach",
   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "If preventing underfilling is the only goal of this PR I would suggest a simpler approach: For example request more addresses than max_addresses and then trim at the end... The current approach doesn't seem minimal and if there is no plan to use it more broadly it seems like overengineering.",
   "request": "",
   "status": "answered",
   "status_by": null,
   "status_note": "reply on record; standing not assessed yet",
   "type": "objection",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/33663#pullrequestreview-3614441070"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-03-20",
   "author": "ajtowns",
   "author_replies": [],
   "clears_with": "answer",
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "retaining banned addresses in AddrMan causes them to compete for slots with un-banned addresses and leads to behavioral differences between fresh and running nodes",
   "hash": "da8236a9e01c7141",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:55:12+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "c:4097004971",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c:4097004971",
   "kind": "approach",
   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "Should we be clearing banned addresses out of addrman? We already skip adding them if they're already banned, so I think it would be consistent.",
   "request": "",
   "status": "open",
   "status_by": null,
   "status_note": "",
   "type": "objection",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/33663#issuecomment-4097004971"
  },
